I like the car analogy and so I'll run with it.

Rememeber the PINTO?

Here was a car, designed by the engineers, promoted by the marketing
people and sold by the sales staff as a great little economical safe
machine, The knid you want to stick your family in and drive around town.
As it turned out, it was a real burner, that is, the gas tank under the
rear seat where your children sat exploded and burned in most accidents.
(I believe I have the essence of the story right).

So here we have Bill Gates and company, promoting and selling the product,
Windows NT as the greatest thing since sliced bread, bar none. The
marketing has been so effective and the heavy handed sales tactics so
good, that the Navy Management buy into it, just like all management
(brainwashed by Byte, or PC World, etc...) would. They insist on Windows
NT and there you go, the YorkTown mess.

Yes, I say basj the product. The PINTO was bashed as a product, wasn't it?

C'mon, most manager read these magazines and get all these 100 secrets, or
250 tips or whatever the writers write and they come in to work the next
day, look at us professionals and say, geez, I know it all now, you don't
have an edge on me, I'm an expert too. Well, in thier arrogance, the
management are failing to realize or understand, they are experts, experts
in management and that technology is not their forte. They are not experts
in technology and a few magazines or a PC at home is not going to make
them an expert and they don't understand this. I don't know why, but I hit
it all the time.

A manager once said to me, you and my son would get along great. He has a
little PC club at home. I was quite insulted by this, I am 42 and his son
is 12 and his sons PC club is active in exchanging stolen software. I
still don't know why he felt that his son had the same knowledge level or
understanding of computers such as I, but I can assure you that I
definately understand the law a damn site better than himself or his son.

A large number of managers are operating under a false assumption that
htey know it all too, and are forcing decisions that are inappropriate on
the rest of us.

rtt

