David Gray wrote:

> We are about to upgrade a from a VAX 4000-60 with VMS 5.5 to a new
> Alpha.Can anyone tell me if the UAF file can simply be copied onto the
> new
> machine, all the directories will be the same so defaults should be no
> problem.
>

As Hoff points out, you should also copy across your rightslist and proxy
files.

There is however a problem with the UAF, in that the quotas required on
Alpha are much larger than for VAX. In my experience, 95% of folks
overlook this.

To estimate appropriate quotas I compare users' existing quotas with the
VAX original values for DEFAULT and SYSTEM. Users with exceptionally high
requirements tend to stand out.

I then look at the quota values for the DEFAULT and SYSTEM accounts on a
newly created Alpha UAF, and go from there.

Good luck!

