>I am curious as what type of CDROM will work with the Dec 5000-240? Is
>there a requirement with the block size (like SUN is 512)? I have a Dec
>expansion chassis that I would like to populate.
>
>I am also looking at using NetBSD Pmax for an OS.  Any pointers out
>there?
>
>Thank You in advance,
>
>John
>
>AA6QN@JUNO.COM
Hy John,
afaik you need a cdrom with 512 sector read enabled for Dec 5000-2xx series
computers, and if you want to boot (ultrix 4.2 / 4.3) some people say you
need
a real dec cdrom because other cdroms will not be accepted by the boot prom.
If you want to use netbsd be careful about the graphics adapter in yout
decstation -
the fastest and best, the pmagc-ca turbo-channel 2d accelerated with intel
processor
is not supported !
Otherwise you will probably want a second hard disk because you need to
reformat
and boot-sector enable it for netbsd and you don t want to do this with the
disk that
has the ultrix system on it ...
Reed the install.html at netbsd.org on the web ...
Happy hacking
Mike





