|>Ive just got hold of a vaxstation, and i need some info about how to get
|>it going. Ive put some ram in, and an old 40meg scsi disk, but im lacking
|>a monitor keyboard. I heard that its possible to control the machines
|>through a dumb term (flicking the S3 switch...) but ive had no luck.
|>

Put the S3 switch in the UP position and plug into the MMJ (DEC423) port
with the little printer icon on it. The port is probably set up for 9600, 8N.


|>There are 8 little yellow led's on the back, which i think are status
|>leds. With no ram in, 0 and 1 dont light up. With eveything set up as
|>above, led '2' (the third from the right) doesnt light up.
|>
|>Does anyone have any idea what these mean? Or where i can find a manual or
|>some info on the web somewhere?
|>

www.dejanews.com can probably find a number of articles detailing the 
various tests and what the numbers mean. You need to get the terminal
working for that to be of any use though - the LEDs are for when you
really, really  want the machine to work :-)

Antonio

