You could bring up DIGITAL UNIX in single user mode from a CD-ROM.

There is nothing you can boot from a floppy, period. Firmware can be
installed from floppy, but this is not a boot, this is a special firmware
load process only.

That said, I have installed Windows NT on a hard drive in a container and
then taken that container to other (different) Alpha's and booted that
same Windows NT. This was done by placing the proper HAL code on a floppy
and then working within the ARC console or ALphaBIOS, pointing to the
proper stuff in the proper places.

