I have successfully put both 2.5 inch (hard to find) or 3.5 inch SCSI
drives in Multias. There are two different sets of mounting hardware:
one which allows 2.5 inch drives and one small PCI card, and one which
allows 3.5 inch devices but no PCI slot. Supposedly, there is an IDE
connector also, but I haven't tried it before, and I am not sure if all
operating systems will support IDE on the Multia.

With 3.5 inch drives, you have to be careful not to get really hot
running or power-hungry drives, as the case is pretty compact and the
power supply is not that strong. If you want massive storage, put the
drive in an external case.

I have a 500 Mb 2.5 inch SCSI drive I could sell if you are interested.
