There is not sufficient information in your note to help you directly.

I will make some comments based on actual circumstances and assume that
you can take these observations and extrapolate to your circumstances.

With all Alpha based systems, if you want to use the Graphics Console, ie;
Monitor, mouse and keyboard, the you must have these items plugged into
the system at Power-Up. Generally, if you Power-Up an Alpha and it fails
to find one or more of these items, it will revert to Serial Console mode,
via COM1.

If you intend to use a Single Keyboard, Single Mouse and Single Monitor
amongst 2 or more Alpha based systems, then you must use a switchbos
mechanism, like those manufactured by Raritan. These units contain phantom
keyboard and mouse circuitry, so thta the machines without a mouse and
keyboard at power-on (say after a power failure) believe themselves to
have such connected when in fact they do not.

There may be other instances where in fact you must use something made by
Raritan called a Gaurdian, these provide phantom capabilities as well.

If trying to make the Mouse, Keyboard and Video cables longer, note,
distances of 10 feet or more can be problematic, due to voltage drop,
noise, insufficient current to operate mouse or keyboard. Video cables
being extended to the lengths or greater usaully require a repeater or
amplifier in circuit and the end results can be somewhat disappointing,
the high frquencies involved do not like mis-matched impedances, lines,
termination and induced noise. The ballast in a Flourescent Light fixture
has such a large magnetic field that it can induce a lot of noise into
Video cables.

rtt

