   of the 21264 simply reduces the interval between the original 0.35 um version
   and the 0.25 um shrink.  Contrast this to the Merced which was always targeted
   at a 0.18 um introduction.  If it had shipped in 1999 it would have had the
   jump on Alpha and the other competitors.  Now it has slipped 8 or 9 months (so
   far) and it will have to face a 0.18 um Alpha instead of the 0.25 um version.

   Even the normally Intel boosting Microprocessor Report is of the opinion that
   the Merced slip has effectively eliminated any chance of Merced gaining the
   performance lead over Alpha or even coming close in integer performance.

