> >> Is there a way to automate this so the ISP gets dialled up without the
> >> hassle of using tip ?. Have had a brief look at the DP4.0 sources, but
> >> a port to DecUnix looks seriously non trivial...
>
> To at least partially answer the actual question - The man page for
> ppp_manual_setup is  a "manual setup" not necessarily manual operation.
> The 'chat' script in the line:
>     pppd /dev/tty01 38400 connect 'chat -v -f /etc/ppp/chat-script'
> should be able to handle the invocation of the dialer. I do not know
> if it will trigger off of IP activity automatically. PPP over ISDN

Charles is correct in pointing out that using the "connect" optionto invoke chat will automatically
invoke the dialer.

 IP activity will be triggered as soon as the modem handshake is successful
and other protocols defined by RFC 1661 (e.g., LCP) are succesfully
negotiated.



--Sowmini




