 A serial mouse and a PS/2 style mouse are somewhat different. And, if it
comes down to wiring, it would appear that your switchbox is wired up for
serial line switching, not really PS/2 mouse switching.


Don't forget, just because the cables plug together that does not mean it
works. 

At this time I'd normally throw in my standard admonishment for MCSE
meaning nothing but drivel and that a real Systems Manager knows what is
going on and what is going to happen before he does it. In other words,
sheesh, we do research to ensure we do it right and that's why we get big
bucks.

The switchbox you are using is liable to zap the Alpha with an ESD spike
in the future at some point and your warranty is null and void with the
use of such a non-approved item. We don't care that it works with a PC or
not, we do all kinds of testing and qualification on options to ensure
systems reliability. That is why you pay a higher price for an Alpha, it
has strong engineering standing with it. If you want to share a single
Monitor, Mouse and Keyboard, the Digital/Compaq approved solution is based
on Raritan technology.

