Actually, you've used HAL a number of times here, but you're way off base.
HAL stands for Hardware Abstraction Layer. This is the essence in the
architecture of Windows NT that seperates the hardware and the kernel.
It is possible you may mean HCL, for Hardware Compatibility List, a
dubious document of terribly interacting devices if I have ever seen one.
With Alpha and VAX systems we test all possible combinations and up until
