|>KA42-B V1.5  (is this a VS3100 model 38, as the front of the case claims?)

Yes. A model 30 would be KA42-A, a model 76 would be KA43.

|>
|>then it goes through the diags countdown (maybe this is not PERFECTLY exact, but
|>something like this):
|>
|>F...E...D...C...B...A...9...8...7...6...5...4_.3_.2_.1?
|>
|> ? 7	80A0 0000.4001
|> ? 6	80A1 0000.4001
|>?? 1	00C0 0011.700E
|>

7 and 6 are the SCSI controllers (7 internal, 6 external). The 0000.4001 bit
means no devices connected; so either you really do have no devices or you
have a connection problem.

1 is the ethernet connection. Make sure that the switch at the back is
set appropriately (AUI or ThinWire) and that there is a network connection
or the appropriate terminator.

|>I know that double question marks means "serious problem", however,
|>I dont have a table of the codes to diagnose it.  Hopefully "1" means
|>"scsi something or other" - this boot was with no SCSI drives attached
|>and the terminator in place on back of the system.
|>

Was the ethernet switch correct? On the M38 I think it is a little push in
switch rather than the big slide switch used on some other systems. There is
a little LED that lights up next to either the AUI or the BNC - make sure the
correct one is selected.


