>As OpenVMS VAX was built for 24x365 operations, standard PC style memory
>designs were not up to the task. Almost all VAX machines were built with
>ECC mmeory architecture. PC memory is so cheap because the memory
>architecture dates back from 1984. VAX systems had very modern memory
>architectures. After all, if you are doing a design for a large
>Hydro-Electric dam, would you not want the system to either fix the memory
>or tell you that a bit was off somewhere during the simulation. On a PC,
>you could build a dam that would not hold back the water with dire
>consequences. Professional Engineers doing simulation work should take
>heed on this point and seriously consider the legal ramifications to you,
>based on the machine you choose to do your design and simulation on.

