Our company has a Priosis ZX 6000 server with 3 storage work towers
connected via 2 Mylex cards. Recently our UPS shutdown due to a fire alarm
causing a dirty shutdown of our system. When supply came back on the RAID
towers did not have a chance to initialise before the server came on.
This caused 2 of the towers (all disks) the be marked as dead. When the dead
disks were brought back on-line the O/S was corrupted which required us to
rebuild the system.

I know that the raid towers should power up for at least 10secs before the
server is switched on but in this situation it is not possible.

Has anyone had this problem before?
We are considering building a time delayed power board to prevent this from
happening again.

