In article <35B7CBA3.FBA7700@intop.net>, "J. S. Havard" <enigma@intop.net> writes:
|>What are they?  All I know is boot.  And I don't know what the switches

Quick guide to the uVAX II console:
	BOOT [/R5:xxxxxxx] [device]
	CONTINUE
	DEPOSIT [qual] address data
	EXAMINE
	FIND
	INITIALIZE
	HALT
	START address
	TEST n
	UNJAM
(there's more but the above should do for now - most later processors
implement the HELP command but the uVAX II doesn't).

Which switches do you mean? 

The console panel on the rear I/O distribution panel has three switches. One
is a rotary switch used to set the console baud rate. One is a rotary to select
RUN (arrow), LANGUAGE INQUIRY (face) or TEST (T in circle). The final one
determines whether a BREAK at the console terminal halts the processor:
dot-outside-circle prevents such halts, dot-inside-circle permits such
halts.

