In article <6p8j6g$ijj$1@nz12.rz.uni-karlsruhe.de>,
  Alexander Schulz <schulz@ira.uka.de> wrote:
> I have found an old DECserver 300. I guess it's a terminalserver from the
> connectors I can see (Ethernet and RJ-45 type, but smaller). Does anyone
> know how to operate such a thing, how to connect something to the ports (it
> seems clear for the ethernet ;-) and what software is needed to run it? Ist
> software still available and can I find some documentation somewhere?

The DS 300 is a 16 port terminal server.  The connectors are MMJs, 6 pin.  To
run it you need to download the terminal software, which is available on the
VMS Layered Products CD set.  DS 300s have been discontinued for quite a few
years but are still common in VMS sites (we have several customers still using
them with new Alphas).  I believe the current software supports both LAT and
Telnet.
