On Fri, 24 Jul 1998 20:10:44 GMT, LaMeR <lamer@aol.com> wrote:
>I recently bought a dec multia 166 off of onsale - what kind of hard
>drive can i put in this - it has no standard internal power connectors
>- it has room for a notebook drive up front and a standard drive in
>the back and it has a small notebook like connector with no cable on
>it. help

It looks like the machine will accept either a 2.5 inch IDE drive or a 3.5
inch, low-profile SCSI disk. That 4-pin connector at the end of the SCSI
interface board is a power connector, with the same pinouts as a floppy
drive (yellow +12 wire on top, two ground wires, red +5 wire on bottom).

Depending on what OS you intend to run on it, I'd recommand a 300-500 MB
drive, minimum. I'd also recommend SCSI over IDE, both because the IDE
extension cable needed is probably hard to find and because SCSI just plain
works better. The machine wants Nx36 true parity RAM, too. (Which is weird,
because the RAM that came with my Alphastation 200 is Nx33; it worked fine
in that machine, but the Multia doesn't see it at all.)



