In article <35B4B6C7.33F51E41@cyberdude.com>, David Gray <davegray@cyberdude.com> writes:
:We are about to upgrade a from a VAX 4000-60 with VMS 5.5 to a new
:Alpha.

  Check the OpenVMS operating system migration documentation.  If you
  are using VAX C, check the DEC C for OpenVMS VAX migration documentation.
  Other packages may/will have equivilent migration documentation.

  [OpenVMS VAX and OpenVMS Alpha are very similar and the vast majority
  of "stuff" ports very easily and quickly.  The documentation helps you
  with the corner cases and the local oddities, and it points out system
  dependencies that are used at a few sites that will have implications
  when extended across architectures.)

:Can anyone tell me if the UAF file can simply be copied onto the new
:machine,
:all the directories will be the same so defaults should be no problem.

  Yes, this can be done.  You'll likely need to bring across the
  RIGHTSLIST.DAT file as well.  Possibly also the proxy database. 
  There's a list of the files that comprise the shared personality
  of the OpenVMS Cluster in the OpenVMS V7.2 SDK version of
  SYLOGICALS.TEMPLATE -- these files can (and are) shared between
  OpenVMS VAX and OpenVMS Alpha nodes.

:If anyone has come accross problems doing this could they pls let me
:know.

  I'd recommend bringing your layered products, tools, and OpenVMS
  versions into line on the VAXstation 4000 model 60 first, then
  porting over to OpenVMS Alpha.

  If you have the option, the use of a mixed-architecture OpenVMS
  Cluster greatly speeds the work -- you can have the same files
  (source, data, etc) available to the OpenVMS VAX and the OpenVMS
  Alpha system, and this will make most any port, and particularly
  an "incremental port", easier.

  Check the layered product software rollout information available
  at: http://www.openvms.digital.com/openvms/os/swroll/index.html


