Both NT and VMS may have difficulties stopping processes.

Under NT, I've run into a number of occasions where Service Control Manager
couldn't stop/start the process because of memory problems caused by that
very same process (in this case, runaway CGI scripts under IIS).  The only
solution was to restart NT.

Under VMS, let me know if you could stop any process in a MUTEX or RWAST
state.  We've had to take down our VAX a number of times because of A1Mail
going into MUTEX because of resource problems (which hopefully we've cleared
by now).

Regards,
Brian Steele


