Jeff Campbell wrote:
> 
> I am trying to copy an RSX-11M V4.2 system from an RL02 disk pack to an
> MSCP disk. Using standalone BRU, the copy/ver completes with no errors.
> BRU reports that the DU: disk is not hardware bootable.
> 
> After booting the RL02 system disk again, I mount the DU: drive and
> attempt to boot the RSX11M.SYS image in DU:[1,54]. The boot doesn't
> happen - the system hangs.
> 
> Help!    8-)
------

You have to recreate the system for the DU drive, boot and save that ...

PIP DU:[1,54]RSX11M.SYS=DU:[1,54]RSX11M.TSK/CO/BL:498.
VMR @SYSVMR
BOO DU:[1,54]RSX11M.SYS

When the system starts

TIM xx:xx xx-xxx-xx
SAV /WB

Now you've got a bootable system disk.

Hope you've got a sysvmr.cmd, else you'll have to work it all out and
enter the commands by hand.

Stuart



