Arne Vajh�j wrote:
> It is true that VMS systems can stay up forever. I will usually
> recommend
> a reboot every 2 or 3 month, not so much to avoid memory leak problems

Actually, the *real* reason to do un-necessary reboots is to ensure that your
system will
reboot properly. Whenever you make changes, you risk causing problems once the
system is rebooted. (eg: manually define a logical name, and forget to have
that logical name defined during the systems startup).

So a regular reboot ensures that you do spot problems under controlled
conditions. This way, when a disaster strikes, you need not worry about that
many things that can go wrong.



