Two things:

1)  VMS and Unix are quite different regarding process creation: Unix
    creates a process for each image activation. VMS does not. Usually
    there is only ONE process creation per login !

2)  The 750 was a low-end system used in the early 1980's !
    I do not think 1000 process creations/second is realistic on that.

