Based on what Microsoft said at the Alpha Processor Inc. launch on June
16, the UK trade rag is misinformed. As I wrote in Shannon Knows DEC
V5N16, June 22, 1998...

Microsoft senior VP Jim Allchin touted the virtues of WNT V5 on Alpha.
Allchin declined to provide a firm release date for WNT 5, but said that
a SDK would be available soon. The oft-delayed V5 release is now
expected sometime in 2HCY99. Although Allchin didn�t cover much new
ground regarding Microsoft�s support for the Alpha architecture, he did
state that work on the full-blown WNT V6 proceeds apace, and that
Microsoft would not tie the release of WNT V5 to any specific
architecture. In other words, Microsoft will not delay the release of
the OS to coincide with the availability of IA64.

Cheers,

