  Probably a pair of RF71 400 MB DSSI disk drives.

:It's in a cabinet...what type?

  The BA213 -- 12 Q-bus slots -- was used for the MicroVAX 3400,
  and the BA215 -- 6 slots -- was used for the MicroVAX 3300.

:It has a tape drive; what type?  (this is a give-a-way)

  TK (common, Q-bus controller) or TF (rare, DSSI-based) series
  CompaTape tape drive, likely either the 50 or the 70 series.

:There's one restriction...your entire package must weigh some 120
:pounds....

  It's been a while since I've lifted a loaded BA213 -- I may be
  able to dig up the official specified weight for the system, if
  it's a concern.  I don't think it's quite as much as 120 pounds,
  but it's heavy enough that most folks will certainly notice it.

