I think a large part of the problem is that the open/integrated nature
of a GUI environment creates more opportunities for people to break
things.  For instance, if I'm designing an entry field for numeric
data, I don't want the user to be able to type text into the field, or
it may break the program.  No problem, but if I move the application
to a GUI environment, maybe some user will try to cut & paste text
data into the numeric-only field; has the program protected itself
against this possiblility?

I think you're right that the basic interactions are the same in both
cases...  There's just more ways to make the interaction happen in one
environment...  :-D


