  A few years ago, around VMS 5.2, there was a leakage problem with
allocation of pages in the page file (1 page remnants of previous
allocations caused the free space in the page file to be "fragmented",
so that future allocations took longer and longer as time went by)
that indeed did cause systems to need to be rebooted every couple of
weeks or so. That problem was fixed a long time ago. So, that expert
was either in the know at the time, or he was just indulging in 
PC-think about the need for frequent reboots.

