Kevin Lai wrote:
> 
> I am new to OpenVMS.
> 
> How can I ensure all new file creation default to a fixed file
> permission?
> 
To set default protection for files in a directory, set a default
protection ACL with a command like this:

$ SET SECURITY X.DIR/ACL=(DEFAULT,SYSTEM:RWED,OWNER:RWED,GROUP:RE,W:RE)

Setting default protection for the current process can be done
with 

$ SET PROTECTION=(prot-code)/DEFAULT

and probably with a SET SECURITY command that I've not yet bothered
to learn.

BTW, comp.os.vms is a better place to ask VMS questions.

