Kent Rankin wrote:
> 
> I bought a lot(group) of vt-320's and lk-201's the other day at a
> university auction for $20.  Six of them mind you.  I am rather happy
> with the deal.  However, when trying to use them, I have a bit of a
> problem.
> Here it goes:
> 
>     The terminal doesn't send anything, nor recieve anything.
> 
> How unusual.  Bet you guys never hear questions about problems like
> that.
> Here is the situation:
> 
>     I have both a Sun 3/50 and a Pentium-based Linux box.  I have a
> cable from the serial port on the terminal to an adapter from the MMJ
> connector to a male DB25 port.
> 
>     Is this adapter for the printer connection?  It is the only one that
> I have, so I need to know if I need to go get another one somewhere.
> And where to get some of them for the other 5 terminals.
> 
>     Are the settings wrong on the terminal?  When I boot up the Sun, the
> Modem DSR status goes to On, and goes to Off when it shuts down.
> 
> Thanks in advance,
> 
> Kent Rankin
----
Normally, you use the DB25 connector labelled COM on the terminal.  If
there is an MMJ connector on the terminal, it is usually for a printer.

Beware a common problem in the cabling is that Tx & Rx (Pins 2 and 3) on
the DB25 end up swapped and you need a null modem.

The terminals will normally work with data leads only.  Check this out
in setup (F3).  Data leads are simply 2,3 and 7.

You don't need to worry about any other signals.

Stuart



