People complain about stability problems with NT. From my
experience (developer's rather than sysadmin's) all NT
stability problems can be attributed to unstable device
drivers. For example, I installed cheap scci card on my
system to connect to MO drive. After that system began
crashing when launching some apps (completely unrelated to
external drive). I uninstalled driver for the card and
crashes never happened after that. Another example: I
installed audio card with the same IRQ (interrupt number) as
NIC: system crashed when I tried to access network.
So, I'm convinced that beyond hardware problems most
problems come from buggy device drivers.
Just curious: on VMS can a buggy audio driver crash OS for
example? How about Unix?

