You generally don't have a console terminal to connect to
the com port. You don't want to need one. It's one of the
reasons you have NT. Most places wouldn't know what to do 
with a character based console on NT. It also keeps the 
machine down longer and you need it up ASAP.

People don't run checked builds unless they are expecting a 
problem such as when developing a drivers. If they were 
expecting a problem during production, they wouldn't be 
using the software. It's supposed to work when you buy it.



