Boris wrote:
> People complain about stability problems with NT. From my
> experience (developer's rather than sysadmin's) all NT
> stability problems can be attributed to unstable device
> drivers. 
...
> So, I'm convinced that beyond hardware problems most
> problems come from buggy device drivers.
> Just curious: on VMS can a buggy audio driver crash OS for
> example? How about Unix?

Buggy device drivers can crash VMS, and I would say around 
50% of the VMS crashes I've seen (not caused by my own
kernel mode code :-) would be driver related.  OTOH, these
bugs are very rare compared to NT.

The big difference is that on VMS I can almost always track
down the crash to the driver, and don't have to resort to
deinstalling code randomly to find the cause.  The OS goes 
to great lengths to ensure that the error log is saved to
disk, and it's easy to wander around the crash dump afterwards 
and do a post mortem.

