An Update to my quest to get USB ports working on my DEC Personal Workstation
200i...........

Since the last time where i managed to get the USB up by installing the
Celebris GL6200DP bios, DEC has released a new BIOS for the PWS 200i, u can
find it @ http://www.workstation.digital.com/drivers/iseries200/i200.html

The new BIOS for the 200i and 180i machines is 1.05.02. here is what the
renotes.txt says. Take note @ the end they mention "USB Support enabled but
not fully tested. USB peripherals may not be hot-plugged is a known
limitation." Just FYi, i haven't had any problems with my USB devices at all
! windows98 works REALLY great on this machine....

hope this helps someone...

                                Release Note
                              ====================

                        Digital Personal Workstation 180i/200i

  Version       :       V1.05.02

  Date          :       June 16, 1998

  Code Base     :       Kauai code base version 1.05.01

  Files Loc  :

                BIOS.ROM        -       256K Binary File
	    BIOS.TXT	  -	    Notes on how to create BIOS diskette
                VGA.ROM         -       E37 Binary File
                PHLASH.EXE      -       Phlash Utility
                PLATFORM.BIN    -       Phlash Utility(without bootblock)
                NVRAM.LST       -       NVRAM List File
                CRISDISK.ZIP    -       Crisis Disk Utilities
                RELNOTES.TXT    -       This File

  Note 1.	    This platform.bin will not phlash bootblock.
                If you want to phlash bootblock please type --
                phlash /PF="BB" bios.rom
                       ^^^^^^^^______________ must be caps.
		    and j27 on the MLB must set to 2-3 position.

  Note 2:       Procedure to create a crisis diskette.

                1. Create an empty directory, for example
                -> MD CRISDISK
                2. Copy CRISDISK.ZIP to CRISDISK.
                3. Change current directory to CRISDISK.
                -> CD CRISDISK
                4. Extract crisdisk.zip
                -> pkunzip crisdisk.zip
                5. We will get a "crisdisk.bat".
                6. Run crisdisk.bat to build a crisis diskette.

		    Instructions to create the bootable BIOS diskette
		    can be found in the User's Guide that came with
		    your Personal Workstation or you can refer to
		    the BIOS.TXT file that is included with this ZIP
		    file.

  Checksum      :

                BIOS.ROM        =       8CC9h
                VGA.ROM         =       F2C9h

  Signon        :

                Digital Personal Workstation 6180 Version 1.05.02
                Digital Personal Workstation 6200 Version 1.05.02

  Following changes are made from BIOS 1.04 to generate BIOS V1.05.02

        o Fixed a problem that prevented the system from booting if
	    the Mouse was disabled in the BIOS setup.

        o Fixed a Year 2000 problem.

        o USB Support enabled but not fully tested. USB peripherals
