> problem goes away, you'd send him packing, wouldn't you? Why do we accept
> this from Microsoft then? We should send them packing, no.

Problem-solving in the Windows world is not like problem-solving in
the VMS/Unix world. It is entirely different. I would label it
"emperical" problem-solving instead of "analytical" problem-solving.

Because Windows has tenths of thousands of undocumented variables in the
registry, then it is impossible to understand what goes on. You simply
learn that if something happends with X then the fastest solution is
to reinstall Y.

Arne



