I sincerely hope what you're doing is trying to build a business case to
determine the best computing platform for your environment.  Although I'm an
NT supporter, I don't always recommend NT (or even MS products) to people if
it doesn't fit their needs.  Not all OS's are good for everything.  As for
your case against NT, I would throw out any problems that aren't
reproducible on NT 4.0  (i.e., the British bank example in this thread),
since earlier versions of NT are no longer available for sale.  On NT4,
before saying there is a problem, make sure that Service Pack 3 doesn't fix
it, since MS recommends applying SP3 to production systems.

One other thing to consider is the current and expected future availability
of support people for whichever OS you choose.  NT is a clear winner here,
as are some variants of Unix.  I'm not so sure about VMS in the US as that
depends a lot on Compaq.  Mainframe support people are also getting harder
to find.

