I created a CD-ROM using mkisofs 1.12b4 -joliet -rational-rock -all-files
(on Solaris 2.6) and wrote the image using cdrecord 1.6 (on Linux 2.0.34).
I have no problems mounting the CD-ROM on Solaris 2.6 or on Windows.
However when I try to mount the CD-ROM under Ultrix 4.4 (on a DECstation
3100 using the same CD-ROM drive as under Solaris) I see:

	# /etc/mount  -t cdfs /dev/rz4c /cdrom 
	cdfs_mount: cannot find root inode
	cdfs_mount: cannot mount /dev/rz4c on /cdrom: Invalid argument

and in the console I see:

	cdfs_ginit: g_number 325632 has 0 vol seq number
	
What is a "vol seq number" and how do I make it non-zero?

When using mkisofs I also specified
	-volid "${volid}" -preparer "$me" -publisher "$me" -appid "$appi" 
and on this particular disk (my first) the volid was something
stupid ("1 (`date`)" in fact).

In the source for mkisofs, I found
	/*
	 * Volume sequence number to use in all of the iso directory records.
	 */
	#define DEF_VSN         1
So the Volume sequence number shouldn't be zero.

Thanks for your help
Stuart



