>stuff will have to be handled. Although user apps don't mess with segment
>registers no more, the OSes do. For example NT uses the FS register as some
>pointer to a thread specific data structure. Hopefully MMX and Katmai
>instructions will transfer relatively simply.


Where is the market for booting an x86 OS on a Merced machine?  The first
ones will cost a lot, at absolute best only be slightly faster (and
probably in reality will be slower) than the fastest x86 machines when
released, and you'll be taking risks with compatibility.  A few years
down the road, when a Merced will be faster at x86 and not as expensive,
OSes will have been ported.  Those that haven't, you'll have to run on
"legacy" x86 hardware.

