Unfortunately, it includes an ominous application warning:
=====
File systems of up to 2^40 bytes (1TB) are supported. A single
file can also consume up to 1TB of disk storage.  Larger capacity
systems require the use and manipulation of larger data files and
file systems.  Huge amounts of storage are becoming common on
servers as disk storage prices drop. The maximum storage of a
UnixWare 7 system current stands at approximately 78,000
Terabytes!  File Systems will automatically support the increased
capacity. Files of greater than 2GB are recommended only for
special applications (usually database) and only a limited number
of system commands are designed to handle files of this size.
=====

What this means is that a bigger dumpster does not guarantee a
cleaner office.  Your application MUST support greater large
pointers or your maximum file size will hit the wall prematurely.

