Bryan Oakley <oakley@channelpoint.com> writes:

>I'm curious about a point of history. I recently read a newsgroup post
>(not here...) from someone who said something like "when they changed
>the name from DEC to Digital when Ken Olsen left...".

>Isn't it correct that the name has *always* been Digital Equipment
>Corporation? Did Digital ever use "DEC" officially? I don't ever recall
>seeing "DEC" on advertisements or manuals or computers, though I'm not
>known to have a strong memory..

Yes, until recently we've always been Digital Equipment Corporation,
but the company tolerated the DEC nickname until after my 1974-1978
stint working on DECsystem-10s in the early DECnet days.  Some time in
the early 80s marketing tried to quash the DEC nickname and get
everyone to use Digital.  Apparently people were getting confused by
seeing digital signs and hearing DEC.  Ten years later people were
still getting confused about hearing Digital so we became DIGITAL.
Finally a year or two ago marketing threw in the towel and
acknowledged that DEC was our nickname but reminded us we were still
DIGITAL.

International quickly followed suit and competition between DEC and IBM
resumed.  :-)
