> I have a new vaxstation 2000 without a monitor.... I would like to

Nice beast, isn't it? The VAX in a wine cask...

> hook up a serial terminal as the console.  How would I do this?  I

You need a VT100 (compatible works, too) or better and a special cable
which connects to the 9-pin female plug with the printer
symbol. Cabling is:

VAX	Terminal
2	3
3	2
7	7
8-9

8-9 means that these pins need to be shorted to tell the VAX to use
this terminal as a console. Terminal settings should be 9k6, 8N1,
software flow control.
 
> have hooked up a non-dec monitor to the kb/mouse/monitor using a bc18p
> cable and, even though the monitor wont sync well, I can see that the
> system passes the self tests and gets a >>> prompt.

Looks fine so far.
 
> On the 5000, there is a command to type to make is switch over to the
> serial port at boot-up.

For booting: B/n DUA[01] where n is 1 for normal boot, 3 for ask
mode.There are several others but these two will suffice.  DUA[01]
means booting from disk #1 or #2, MUA0 from tape or ESA0 from the
network. For network boot you'll obviously need a MOP-server.

