Subject: How to get Service Name on ASE Cluster?
Date: 1998/07/08
Message-ID: <35A33C39.3E6B86FD@datenrevision.de>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 369504674
Cache-Post-Path: stationfall!unknown@internetserver.datenrevision.de
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: datenrevision GmbH
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Hi,
we are running 2 instances of an application on an ASE Cluster using DU
4.0. The cluster environment defines 2 "services" (virtual machines),
which are each dedicated to one instance of the application. We connect
to the virtual machines by telnet. But our Login accounts are set up on
the cluster, so we physically have just one Login Directory and profile.
In order to correctly set up our environment in the profile, we need the
information, to which of the virtual machines we are connected. But we
only can get the names of the physical machines (hostname, etc.), which
we are not interested in.
Does anybody know how to get the name or identification of the virtual
machine (i.e. ASE "service")?

Thanks



