Hi everyone, further to my last post here. The biggest clue i got was that the
200i Personal Workstations were very similar in motherboard with the Celebris
GL6200 DP series.

I hunted down the latest 6200DP bios, which was 1.02 @
http://www.windows.digital.com/ntsbuftp/index/epid49.htm
installed it over the version 1.04 bios for my 200i...

almost had a heart attack when the BIOS flasher reported an error and asked
for a crisis disk (which i had NOT created)...

rebooted the machine after the error message, went into the BIOS setup, seemed
normal, USB ports ENABLED !!! reset everything to the defaults i like, saved
it, rebooted and hey windows98 discovers the Intel USB ports !!!!! i've got
them running for at least 5 days now, no problems so far, seems to be normal,
the BIOS has everything the 1.04 bios had (1.02 for GL6200 had a newer date on
it tho... so much for DEC version numbers)

so for those with the PWS 200i, using Windows98, and want the USB ports,
install the GL6200DP bios 1.02 !!!

it was, afterall, a software switch....

hope this helps someone else as well.. 8)

cheers

