rivie@rivie.daautah.com (Roger Ivie) writes:

> 
> Most folks I know took a work holiday for the 4th of July on the 3rd (since 
> the 4th was Saturday). Sure looked like a date-adjustment to me...
> 

Well, sort of.  In years when July 4th falls M-F, that day is usually a
holiday.  When it falls on Saturday or Sunday, the nearest weekday is
often substituted as a work holiday (depends on the employer, of course,
but most follow this practice).

Some companies will extend to a 4-day weekend if July 4th falls on
Tuesday or Thursday.  This usually works OK because the "spare" holiday
can float between Christmas and Independence Day to make one of them a
4-day weekend.  (Sometimes both will fall on weekend days, as will
happen in 1999--that usually means either a floating holiday for the
employee, or a long weekend for one of the above "normal" holidays)
