Some month ago there was a report about the chip manufacturing in a german
computer magazine c't ( http://www.ct.heise.de/ ). What Intel does was called
the 'copy all' model. If they build a new plant, they make an exact copy of
what they have already running. One nice example:

If there is a pipe that must be passed around something like this:

-------\  O  /---
