Does anyone know if there is such a monster for Alpha machines?  We have AXPs
based on PCI/EISA and Turbochannel.  What I'm looking for is something similar
to a DAS FDDI card.  There are two ports sharing the same MAC address.  If one
port goes out (ie the hub goes out, etc) it automatically switches to the
second port seamlessly without any intervention from the OS.  Compaq 7000
machines have this capability, though it's on an imbedded NIC.

We're also looking at something like this for 6000/7000 class Vaxen, though
the Alphas are our primary concern.

Any help is appreciated.

-Richard



