APC's powerchute software (v1.2) is in the first case.  The program
works just fine under V6.x but before we upgraded, we found that v7.x
is not now nor will it ever be supported (according to several
different people at APC, they know there is a problem and not enough
interested parties to repair/replace it)

I tried it after the upgrade anyway, just to see what the problems
would be.  It turns out as soon as the UPS goes into battery mode and
sends the message to all users, the console gets corrupted and only
comes back after a power cycle (or incidently on a set term which was
in our startup). 

If the system goes on battery, prints the message and then power is
restored, it means either no console until the next convienient reboot
or a forced reboot while production is trying to recover from the
power loss.  Neither solution is great, but we will live with it until
we can seek an alternative.

