  V7.1-2 will be required.  Sorry.  It is highly unlikely that any
  new platforms will ever be offered on a V6.2 baseline, unless they
  happen to be functionally equivalent to a platform already supported
  on V6.2-xxx.

  The current mainline version of OpenVMS is V7.1 and its varients
  (V7.1-1H1, V7.1-1H2) - we plan to continue new support for V7.1-xxx
  systems at least thru the year 2000 - even after new functional
  releases (for example V7.2) are released.  We made a lot of changes
  in V7.1 to allow new system platforms and devices to be added to
  OpenVMS without needing to re-master OpenVMS - and it should provide
  us with much more flexibility than we currently have with V6.2-xxx.

  I hope you are able to upgrade to V7.1-xxx, as it is IMHO a very
  stable, and feature rich version.  Are you stuck because of device
  drivers or applications that for some other reason will not run on
  V7.1?



