Timothy Cullip apparently asked:

: If a person purchases a Digital Personnal Workstation (PWS) 600a
: (the "a" indicating it is an MS NT machine), can he in the future
: convert it to Digital Unix (in effect making it a 600au) by just
: a software change?

  The DPWS 600a and all other -a series DPWS systems are not recognized
  by the SRM firmware necessary to run OpenVMS and Compaq's Digital UNIX
  -- the -a series systems are Microsoft Windows NT systems (only)...

  If you want to swap between Windows NT, OpenVMS, and/or Compaq's Digital
  UNIX, you need a DPWS-au series system.  (And I/O controllers that are
  supported by each of the operating systems you plan to run, of course.)

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
