the VMS house would be a 200 story high rise with a 30,000 car garage,
a helipad, a marina, an airport, and a rail station in the basement.
However, you'd need to come and go by approved transportation- no private
cars, though the bus system and subway would be excellent. You would
not be given access to the ground, though.
If you wanted your own garden, the building manager would give you a flowerpot,
assuming that your quota would cover it. dirt would cost extra.
Apartments would be large, not to be roomy, but because this way you have to
walk a lot to get anywhere to be sure you arent just going there by mistake.
It would take so long to walk to get a snack that most people would
just sit and be hungry because otherwise they'd get sore feet.
Everybody living in the VMS house would have carpal tunnel syndrome.
You woudnt find any doors, because to go from
room to room you'd have to SET the DEFAULT door to go through first. :)
You'd have to have an oration contest before you could use anything,
and you'd need special security privileges to flush the toilet. 
It would be excellent as a hotel where you present no access to the
guest, but it'd be a terribly inconvenient place to live.
The place would have a staff of 400 to keep it going. 
Each floor would have its own janitors to avoid a deadlock where there
werent aenough janitors to clean a floor up.
You woudlnt be able to get to the kitchen; you'd have a chef whose
name was about twice as long as the longest indian or greek name,
who would be the one with the authority to cook things and make you
what you wanted. He'd only respond if you called him by name.
 however, you coudlnt just ask for a burger- he'd come right back and 
hand you an empty bun unless you gave him the right /LETTUCE and /BEEF
flags. Oddly enough, it would be quite permissible to rent furniture which
had some option to also contain lettuce or beef, because everyone supports
the same flags. 
In case of intruders, which admittedly might be rare, you'd have no way
of defending yourself because you woudlnt have permission to get to the
guns, since only the house manager would be. 
You wouldnt have to do laundry, though, or ever throw anythign away-
you'd just get a new version of your clothes, magazines, or garbage,
as soon as you updated the existing version. However, you wouldnt
be able to throw something away more than 32,767 times. 
Also, your rent would cost millions and millions of dollars, and the only
thing which would cost more would be the IBM house up the street. 
(which would need to be water-cooled and you woudlnt be able to buy an
apartment, only lease)
There would be permission on everything, and little tags hanging on
all the drawers with a long list of people who should and shouldnt be
in there, and even things in the open like the sofa would not be something
you could just sit down on. 
The locks on the front door wouldnt just be normal locks with a key, since
somebody might have copied the key, and at any rate there would be somebody
with the ability to pick the lock or have a skeleton key, so instead there
would be a combination lock. However, it would have 30 5 digit numbers in the
combo and it would be changed monthly, so you'd often find yourself out in
the rain waiting for the house manager to let you in. 
(and then you'd have to spend a long time talking to your dry clothes 
describing them in detail before you could put them on and dry off.)
There would be no light switches, valves, controls, buttons, or levers.
Everythign would be voice controlled, but you'd get hoarse changing the
channel on the tv. 
There woudl be no AC outlets- why would you need one when you arent allowed 
to use your own appliances?
And finally, unless you had prior approval from the building manager,
owning a screwdriver, drill, or other tool, woudl be strictly
prohibited.






